# `make fit` (ADR-0038): the netlist it places, nextpnr's log -- which IS the
# measurement, so keep it around to read -- and the yosys log, kept out of the
# terminal so no yosys cell count is ever mistaken for an area number.
fit.json
fit.log
fit.synth.log
# `make soc-timing` (ADR-0054): the SoC netlist, the placed bitstream ASCII, the
# three logs and the `icetime` report. soc.pnr.log and soc.timing.rpt ARE the
# measurement, so they are kept on disk to read -- and never committed, because
# a checked-in timing report is a number that stops tracking the RTL.
soc.json
soc.asc
soc.synth.log
soc.pnr.log
soc.timing.rpt
soc.icetime.log
# `make ecp5-timing`: the ECP5 netlist, the Trellis text configuration, the two
# logs and nextpnr's own JSON report. Same rule as the soc.* files above -- the
# report and the placement log ARE the measurement, so they stay on disk to
# read, and are never committed. There is no bitstream here: `--textcfg` is
# written as the "expressible in the target's configuration" check and nothing
# packs it.
ecp5.json
ecp5.config
ecp5.report.json
ecp5.synth.log
ecp5.pnr.log
# The de-interleaved ROM banks `make soc-rom` writes from a test program. Build
# artifacts of whichever SOC_PROG was last built, not source.
soc/rom_even.hex
soc/rom_odd.hex
# `make compare-timing`: two netlists, two placements, the logs and the icetime
# reports. Same rule as the soc.* files above -- the reports ARE the measurement
# and are kept on disk to read, and never committed, because a checked-in timing
# report is a number that stops tracking the RTL.
compare.*.json
compare.*.asc
compare.*.log
compare.*.rpt
compare.vvp
soc/compare/rom_even.hex
soc/compare/rom_odd.hex
soc/compare/rom_flat.hex
# `make compare-dhrystone`: the benchmark's image in both cores' ROM shapes, the
# data RAM both start from, and the simulation that runs them.
compare.dhry.vvp
soc/compare/dhry_even.hex
soc/compare/dhry_odd.hex
soc/compare/dhry_flat.hex
soc/compare/dhry_ram.hex
# `soc/depth/`: the spike's netlists, placements, logs and icetime reports, plus
# the memory it generates from rtl/imemory.v and the runner it patches out of
# test/cxxrtl.cc. Same rule as the soc.* and compare.* files above -- the reports
# ARE the measurement and are kept on disk to read, and never committed.
depth.out/
depth.*.csv
# `soc/baseline_sweep.sh`: one report, bitstream and placement log per seed, plus
# the CSV whose header states the tree and the toolchain they were measured on.
# Same rule again -- the reports ARE the measurement, kept on disk to read and
# never committed, because a checked-in timing report is a number that stops
# tracking the RTL.
baseline.out/
# `make netlist-digest` / `netlist-diff` / `netlist-determinism`: the canonical
# netlists both sides of a comparison, the shipping ones the control places, its
# three bitstreams and logs, and the mutated copy of the tree it builds. The
# canonical netlist in here is a classifier and NOT a design -- it is not what
# ships, and it places to a different bitstream, so nothing may hand it to
# nextpnr.
netlist.out/
formal/riscv-formal
formal/riscv-formal.tmp
formal/complete
formal/complete_cover
formal/cover
formal/checks
formal/dmemcheck
formal/imemcheck
formal/components_*
formal/components
formal/pcloop_cover
# `make -C formal remeasure-fg`: the one-line-[depth] copy of checks.cfg the
# sweep writes, and the single-check set it generates from it. Both are rebuilt
# from checks.cfg on every run.
formal/fg-probe.cfg
formal/fg-probe/
# `make -C formal traps-region-probe`: the two mutated cores it proves the
# region cause arm against, and their sby workdirs. Rebuilt from rtl/ and
# formal/traps.sv on every run.
formal/region-probe/
__pycache__/
test/rtl.cc
test/monitor.sim.v
*.vvp
*.vcd
disasm.s
disasm.o
rvfi_macros.vh
.hdl_checker
.emacs/
a.out.dSYM/
obj_dir/
rtl/rom.mem
sim
sim.dSYM/
# The Sail co-simulation runner: a second cxxrtl binary, and not on `make
# test`'s path.
cosim
cosim.dSYM/
# `make sail-setup` and `make lint-setup` unpack into a cache outside the
# checkout, so a git worktree sees the same install the main checkout does.
# tools/ stays ignored so an install an older checkout left behind here can
# never be committed.
tools/
test/a.out.dSYM/
# Swarm agent worktrees (.claude/tracker.json stays tracked).
.claude/worktrees/
